9. Interest and Fees
SECTION:
The Borrower shall pay interest on the outstanding principal balance of the Loan at the rate of 3% per annum, calculated on a 360-day year basis. The interest shall be payable monthly in arrears, together with any other fees or charges due under this Agreement. The Lender reserves the right to charge the Borrower any reasonable fees and expenses incurred in connection with the Loan, including, without limitation, legal fees, appraisal fees, and closing costs. The Borrower shall be responsible for the payment of all such fees and expenses.

10. Termination
TEXT:
Upon the occurrence of any of the following events, this Agreement may be terminated:

a. Default by the Borrower in the payment of any amount due under this Agreement when due, or any other default under any of the terms, covenants or conditions of this Agreement;

b. The Borrower becoming insolvent, making an assignment for the benefit of creditors, or filing a petition under any bankruptcy or insolvency law, or having a receiver or trustee appointed for it or any substantial part of its assets;

c. The Borrower failing to perform any of its obligations under this Agreement and failing to cure such default within thirty (30) days after receipt of written notice from the Lender specifying the default and requiring it to be cured;

d. The Borrower ceasing to conduct business in the ordinary course, or taking any action that would reasonably be expected to result in the termination of its business.

In the event of termination, the Borrower shall immediately pay to the Lender all amounts then due and owing under this Agreement, including any unpaid principal, accrued and unpaid interest, and any fees or expenses incurred by the Lender in connection with the termination. The Borrower shall also deliver to the Lender all documents and property of the Lender then in its possession or control.

11. Replayment Terms
TEXT:
The Borrower shall repay the Loan in accordance with the following terms:

(a) Monthly payments of [amount] shall be made by the Borrower to the Lender on the first day of each calendar month, starting [date].

(b) Each payment shall consist of the following amounts:

   (i) The principal amount of the Loan, which shall be repaid in [duration] equal monthly installments;

   (ii) Interest on the outstanding principal balance of the Loan at the rate of 3% per annum, calculated on the basis of a 360-day year; and

   (iii) Any fees or expenses incurred by the Lender in connection with the Loan.

(c) If any payment due under this Agreement is not made when due, the Borrower shall pay to the Lender interest on the overdue amount at the rate of 5% per annum, calculated on the basis of a 360-day year, from the due date until the date of payment.

(d) The Borrower may prepay all or any part of the Loan at any time without penalty, provided that the Borrower gives the Lender at least [duration] days' prior written notice of its intention to do so.

(e) If the Borrower prepays the Loan, it shall pay to the Lender an amount equal to any unamortized fees and expenses incurred by the Lender in connection with the Loan.

(f) If the Borrower fails to make any payment when due under this Agreement, the Lender may declare the entire outstanding principal balance of the Loan, together with all accrued and unpaid interest and fees, immediately due and payable.

(g) The Borrower shall make all payments under this Agreement in United States Dollars.

(h) All payments under this Agreement shall be made to the Lender's account at Banco Santander S.A., 8135 Terri Lock Suite 767, North Stacy, NE 62207, United States of America.

